kai: Heads-up 1 - opened docs PR to unify streaming + cursor-pagination snippets across py/ts/go. Need tiny canonical examples and to fix a stale link in examples/pagination.md.

mina: I can own Python. Prefer sync generator showing resume cursor + retry backoff. Keep it runnable in snippet CI.

ash: I'll draft TypeScript async iterator with inline exponential backoff (2 retries). Short and self-contained.

lisa: Go should show ctx + Recv loop and a short note about cancellation. Keep examples under 12 lines.

link-bot: scan complete 1 - found stale link in examples/pagination.md -> /sdk/old-pagination. Suggested replacement: /sdk/pagination.

kai: Nice. Quick drafts:
mina: ```python
def stream_with_retry(client, prompt, cursor=None):
    for attempt in range(3):
        try:
            for ch in client.generate_stream(prompt, cursor=cursor):
                yield ch
            return
        except Exception:
            if attempt==2: raise
            time.sleep(2**attempt * 0.1)
```

ash: ```ts
async function streamWithRetry(client, prompt, cursor){
  for(let i=0;i<3;i++){
    try{ for await (const c of client.generateStream({prompt,cursor})) console.log(c.text); return }
    catch(e){ if(i===2) throw e; await new Promise(r=>setTimeout(r,2**i*100)) }
  }
}
```

lisa: ```go
func StreamWithRetry(ctx context.Context, c *redwood.Client, prompt, cursor string) error {
  for i:=0;i<3;i++{
    s, err := c.GenerateStream(ctx, prompt, cursor)
    if err!=nil{ time.Sleep(time.Duration(1<<i)*100*time.Millisecond); continue }
    for { ch, err := s.Recv(); if err==io.EOF { return nil }; if err!=nil { break }; fmt.Print(ch.Text) }
  }
  return errors.New("stream failed")
}
```

kai: Excellent. Action items: mina push python commit, ash push ts, lisa push go. I'll patch the stale link as part of the PR and add a one-line migration note about cursor semantics (cursor points to last-committed token; resumes are best-effort). After CI snippet-check passes, merge.
